<VI _name="lvdqmh_script_new_event.vi" description="Headless DQMH Create New Event. Adds ONE event to ONE DQMH module in the ACTIVE project by calling Delacor's own scripting VIs as STATIC subVIs - no dialog and no keystroke.\0A\0AChain\3A Parse Project for DQMH Modules.vi -> pick the module by NAME -> Get All Events in Module.vi (the variant Delacor's event dialog uses) -> Script New Event.vi -> Close Scripting References.vi on every parsed module that Script New Event.vi did not already close.\0A\0AWHY ONE HIERARCHY. Module Info carries thirteen refnums that LabVIEW releases when the VI that opened them stops\2C so the parse and the scripter must be subVIs of one running VI.\0A\0ADRY RUN BY DEFAULT. Script? FALSE parses and reports only. Scripting also needs the module found\2C and no locked module in the project. Unsaved modules do not block\2C exactly as Delacor's own event dialog leaves that output unwired. Scripted? says whether Script New Event.vi was called.\0A\0ANO MODAL DIALOG ON PURPOSE. Delacor's dialog runs Check if OK to Proceed.vi\2C Preflight Main VI.vi and Verify Event Names.vi first\3B each opens a modal dialog when its check fails\2C and a modal stops LabVIEW's gRPC service. They are NOT called here\3B the caller must make those checks before Script? is TRUE. Script New Event.vi is never called with an error on its input\2C because it ends in Simple Error Handler.vi.\0A\0AARGUMENT CARRIERS. Arguments VI Path and Reply Payload VI Path name VIs whose front panels hold one control per argument and nothing else. Script New Event.vi moves those controls into the argument clusters\2C closes both references and DELETES both files\2C so pass fresh copies every time. The reply carrier may be empty.\0A\0ARequires DQMH installed and a project OPEN AND ACTIVE in the IDE. Generated by LabVIEWMCP\3B the Delacor VIs it calls belong to the user's DQMH installation and are not shipped with it.">
